 "article": {
  "title": "Traditions That Still Matter",
  "topic": "文化传承与现代生活",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": [
   "neighbour",
   "digital",
   "harmony",
   "difficulty",
   "brake",
   "vacuum",
   "endure",
   "substance",
   "thread",
   "scarf",
   "institution",
   "fabric",
   "railway",
   "custom",
   "pension",
   "possess",
   "feature",
   "reduce",
   "automatic",
   "unnecessary",
   "stadium",
   "visible",
   "ignorant",
   "maintenance",
   "tobacco",
   "divide",
   "modest",
   "whisper",
   "variety",
   "grain",
   "explosive",
   "origin",
   "x-ray",
   "canal",
   "shade",
   "orchestra",
   "guidance",
   "hence",
   "inevitable",
   "rival",
   "purchase",
   "wander",
   "craft",
   "whisky",
   "shelf",
   "chart",
   "granddaughter",
   "submit",
   "resident",
   "triumph"
  ],
  "paras": [
   "In a world of digital speed, traditions still shape who we are. A family custom, a hand-woven fabric, a village festival: these quiet habits connect us to our origin. They remind us where we come from and offer guidance when life becomes difficult. Far from being unnecessary, they give daily life a sense of harmony and belonging.",
   "Take the making of grain-based food as an example. For centuries, farmers have followed the same rhythm: sow in spring, harvest in autumn, and share the crop with neighbours. Each generation adds something modest of its own, keeping the substance of the practice alive. Schools and museums, as institutions, help preserve such traditions and pass them to the young.",
   "Tradition also appears in modern life. Railways that once carried grain from villages to cities now carry travellers who wander far from home. A grandmother may whisper an old recipe to her granddaughter, while a craftsman turns a simple shelf into a work of art. These threads of memory make our cities richer and more humane. Without them, life would lose its variety and charm.",
   "Of course, not every custom deserves to endure. Some old habits divide people and should be changed with courage. The wise approach is to keep what is valuable and submit the rest to honest review. As the composer Gustav Mahler said, \"Tradition is not the worship of ashes, but the preservation of fire.\" We should preserve the fire, not the ashes."
  ],
  "zh": "在数字速度的世界里，传统依然塑造着我们是谁。一个家庭的风俗、一块手工编织的布料、一个乡村节日：这些安静的习惯把我们与自己的来处相连。它们提醒我们来自哪里，并在生活艰难时给予指引。它们绝非多余，反而赋予日常生活一种和谐感与归属感。以谷物食品的制作为例。几个世纪以来，农民遵循同样的节奏：春天播种，秋天收获，与邻居分享收成。每一代人都添加一点属于自己的朴素内容，使这一做法的实质保持鲜活。学校和博物馆作为制度性机构，帮助保存这些传统并传递给年轻人。传统也出现在现代生活中。曾经把谷物从村庄运往城市的铁路，如今载着远离家乡的旅行者。祖母可能向孙女低声传授一道老菜谱，而工匠把一块普通搁板变成艺术品。这些记忆的丝线让我们的城市更丰富、更有人情味。没有它们，生活将失去多样性与魅力。当然，并非每种风俗都值得延续。一些旧习惯分裂人群，应当被勇敢地改变。明智的做法是保留有价值的东西，把其余交给诚实的审视。正如作曲家古斯塔夫·马勒所说：“传统不是对灰烬的崇拜，而是对火种的保存。”我们应当保存火种，而不是灰烬。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "Tradition is not the worship of ashes, but the preservation of fire.",
    "cn": "传统不是对灰烬的崇拜，而是对火种的保存。",
    "why": "not ... but ... 并列对比结构，worship/preservation 为抽象名词化；出自作曲家马勒的名言，可直接用作作文引语。"
   },
   {
    "en": "These threads of memory make our cities richer and more humane.",
    "cn": "这些记忆的丝线让我们的城市更丰富、更有人情味。",
    "why": "threads of memory 为比喻用法；make + 宾语 + 形容词宾补（make our cities richer）是高频写作结构。"
   },
   {
    "en": "The wise approach is to keep what is valuable and submit the rest to honest review.",
    "cn": "明智的做法是保留有价值的东西，把其余交给诚实的审视。",
    "why": "不定式作表语 to keep ... and submit ...；what 引导名词性从句；submit A to B（把A提交给B）为高级搭配。"
   }
  ],
